# Transcripts are data, not source. They are fetched verbatim by the browser and
# parsed a line at a time, so they must arrive as recorded -- the same bytes on a
# Windows clone, a Linux clone, and from whatever serves them. With core.autocrlf=true
# and no rule here, a Windows checkout rewrites every line ending in the bundled
# sample, which is not something a data file should pick up on its way through git.
*.jsonl -text
